        "description": "Reports what a rule would decide for an email you describe: its sender, recipients, subject, plain text and attachment types, and optionally whether it is automated or from a mailing list and its spam score. The email is classified the way received mail is, and the rule's conditions and its own questions are decided as they would be for received mail with that content and those signals, received now. Without them it is not automated and not from a mailing list; a rule that reads a spam score you gave none for is decided on no score, and spam_score is listed in unset_columns. Nothing is stored: no email, classification or decision. Test an unsaved tree from a compile response, or a saved rule by rule_id (its current version). The answer includes what the classifier read from the email. Needs mail:read, a credential acting as a member with their full access (API keys, agent keys and narrowed tokens are refused), and the email rules feature on the organization.",
