        "summary": "Mark a thread read up to a message",
        "description": "Moves the signed-in member's read cursor for this thread forward to the named message or instant, for every device the member uses. Monotonic and idempotent: a position at or behind the stored cursor changes nothing (`advanced: false`), so devices reporting reads out of order converge on the furthest one. Returns the thread's read state after the write; a retry at the same position returns the current state with `advanced: false`. A thread the caller can see no message in answers 404, exactly as an unknown thread. Once the write commits the answer is always 200: if the unread count cannot be read afterwards, `unread_count` is null and `state_unavailable` is true, and the cursor fields still hold. Only a signed-in organization member (a dashboard session or an OAuth member grant) can use this. Organization API keys, agent connection keys and Functions are refused with 403: read state is personal to a member.",
