        "description": "Keep, narrow or revoke one suspended or flagged item. Keeping it, and revoking an API key, needs the decider to cover it (revoking an uncovered key is refused with `grant_forbidden`, `target_not_covered`). Keeping an API key rotated (`rotate: true`, other than the shared Function key) also revokes its older secrets still in a rotation overlap, and needs keys:manage on both the credential and the person: without it, or if the decider lost members:manage meanwhile, it is refused with `grant_forbidden` (`keys_manage_required` or `actor_access_changed`) and nothing is rotated. Person only: a dashboard session, or the person's own OAuth or CLI token with a session step-up of purpose `suspensions.decide` (the person confirms at the step_up_url a 403 step_up_required answer carries, which names this client, then send the token in the Primitive-Step-Up header; the token works only with the client it was confirmed for). Needs members:manage. API keys are refused.",
